cff-version: 1.2.0
title: CorpusMind Voice — Local-First Audio-to-Corpus Pipeline
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the
  metadata provided.
type: software
authors:
  - name: Mandour
    given-names: Waleed
    website: https://waleedmandour.org/
identification:
  abstract: >-
    CorpusMind Voice is a companion tool to CorpusMind, a local-first
    research environment for corpus linguistics and multimodal discourse
    analysis. It converts MP3/MP4/WAV recordings or live microphone input
    into a linguistically annotated corpus entirely offline: ASR with
    word-level timestamps and confidence (faster-whisper large-v3, INT8),
    forced alignment (Montreal Forced Aligner with Arabic and English
    pronunciation dictionaries), prosodic features (Parselmouth/Praat F0,
    intensity, jitter, shimmer, HNR), disfluency detection (pauses,
    fillers, repeats, false starts, interruptions, lengthenings), and
    structured output as SQLite (three tables), pandas-ready JSON and
    TEI/XML with an embedded teiHeader. No data leaves the user's machine
    and no cloud APIs are used.
  keywords:
    - corpus linguistics
    - speech transcription
    - forced alignment
    - prosody
    - disfluency
    - Arabic corpus annotation
    - TEI XML
    - offline natural language processing
  version: "1.0.0"
  repository-code: "https://github.com/waleedmandour/CorpusMind"
  url: "https://waleedmandour.org/projects/CorpusMind/"
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-09-08"
